AWS-017 — Workflow Federation

Document ID: AWS-017
Title: Workflow Federation
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Workflow Federation Model (CWFM) for the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The Canonical Workflow Federation Model establishes the principles, architecture, governance, trust relationships, and coordination mechanisms required for multiple autonomous Atlas organizations to collaboratively execute engineering workflows while preserving sovereignty, interoperability, accountability, and execution integrity.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Workflow federation architecture
Federation participants
Cross-domain execution
Trust relationships
Delegated execution
Workflow exchange
Federation governance
Federation lifecycle

This specification applies to every federated workflow environment.

3. Canonical Definition

Workflow Federation is the governed coordination of workflow execution across two or more autonomous Atlas governance authorities through explicit federation agreements while preserving organizational independence, workflow integrity, and execution traceability.

Workflow Federation coordinates execution across organizations.

It SHALL NOT eliminate organizational sovereignty.

4. Objectives

The Workflow Federation Model SHALL:

Enable cross-organization workflow execution.
Preserve workflow autonomy.
Support trusted workflow exchange.
Enable distributed engineering programs.
Preserve governance integrity.
Support regulatory cooperation.
Maintain execution traceability.
Enable scalable execution ecosystems.
5. Federation Principles

Every workflow federation SHALL satisfy the following principles.

Organizational Sovereignty

Each federation participant SHALL retain governance authority over its own Workflow Definitions and Workflow Instances.

Explicit Trust

Trust relationships SHALL be explicitly declared.

Implicit execution trust SHALL NOT exist.

Semantic Preservation

Federated workflows SHALL preserve canonical Atlas workflow semantics.

Accountability

Each participant SHALL remain accountable for workflows executed under its authority.

Traceability

Cross-organizational workflow execution SHALL remain permanently reconstructable.

Governed Participation

Participation SHALL require an approved Federation Agreement.

6. Federation Participants

Atlas recognizes the following participant types.

Participant	Description
Atlas Constitutional Authority	Constitutional oversight
Government Authority	Public-sector execution
Organization	Enterprise participant
Project Authority	Program execution
Contractor	External execution partner
Supplier	Supply-chain participant
Digital Twin	Federated operational participant
AI Agent	Authorized autonomous participant

Additional participant types MAY be introduced through governed profiles.

7. Federation Agreements

Every federation SHALL define:

Property	Description
Federation ID	Unique identifier
Participating Organizations	Federation members
Trust Model	Trust relationships
Execution Scope	Federated responsibilities
Workflow Exchange Rules	Shared workflow constraints
Delegation Rules	Authority delegation
Review Schedule	Governance review

Federation Agreements SHALL be governed Canonical Atlas Objects.

8. Trust Relationships

Atlas defines the following canonical trust relationships.

Relationship	Description
Full Trust	Workflow execution accepted
Conditional Trust	Execution requires validation
Limited Trust	Restricted workflow exchange
Observation	Visibility without execution authority
No Trust	Workflow exchange prohibited

Trust SHALL remain directional unless explicitly declared reciprocal.

9. Workflow Exchange

Federated participants MAY exchange:

Workflow Definitions
Workflow Interfaces
Workflow Packages
Workflow Programs
Workflow Templates
Execution Status
Completion Notifications
Canonical Events

Workflow exchange SHALL preserve artifact identity and governance metadata.

10. Delegated Execution

Federation MAY delegate authority for:

Workflow execution
Workflow monitoring
Resource allocation
Activity coordination
Recovery execution
Emergency operations

Delegation SHALL define:

Delegating authority
Receiving authority
Delegated scope
Effective period
Revocation conditions

Delegation SHALL NOT transfer constitutional authority.

11. Cross-Domain Execution

Workflow Federation SHALL support execution across:

Organizations
Engineering disciplines
Geographic regions
Regulatory jurisdictions
Cloud environments
Edge environments
Digital Twins
AI ecosystems

Cross-domain execution SHALL preserve local governance obligations.

