Federation history SHALL remain permanently reconstructable.

13. Federation Governance

Every federation SHALL define:

Federation authority
Governance board
Membership rules
Workflow sharing rules
Delegation policies
Dispute resolution process
Audit requirements

Governance SHALL remain independently auditable.

14. Federation Quality

Every workflow federation SHALL satisfy:

Trustworthiness
Transparency
Accountability
Interoperability
Traceability
Execution consistency
Auditability
Scalability

Quality SHALL be continuously evaluated.

15. Federation Events

Federation activities MAY generate Canonical Events.

Examples include:

Federation Established
Organization Joined
Organization Suspended
Workflow Shared
Workflow Delegated
Execution Transferred
Federation Dissolved

Events SHALL conform to ADS-006 — Canonical Event (CEV).

16. Conformance

A Workflow Federation implementation conforms if it:

Supports governed federation agreements.
Preserves organizational autonomy.
Implements canonical trust relationships.
Supports delegated execution.
Preserves workflow identity during exchange.
Maintains federation traceability.
Supports audit-ready execution governance.
17. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

AI-negotiated federation agreements.
Dynamic trust scoring.
Autonomous cross-organization orchestration.
Federated workflow optimization.
Real-time execution synchronization.
International engineering workflow networks.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical workflow federation semantics.

